The townsfolk also painted a grim picture of the Red Bands, a gang terrorizing Phandalin who had murdered a man named Theldender in broad daylight and caused his family to vanish.

00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:25.440
Suspicion fell on Halia of the Miner's Exchange for her curious immunity to the gang's violence.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:39.439
The following morning, the party visited retired adventurer Daran Edermath, who confirmed that the Red Bands operated out of Tresendar Manor under a leader called Glasstaff and warned of undead activity and the ancient ruins of the old well.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:47.520
After receiving a blessing at the Shrine of Luck from Sister Garaele, the party set out along the goblin trail toward the cave where Gundren was believed to be held.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.280
The journey proved treacherous.

00:00:49.439 --> 00:00:56.719
Zenvon narrowly avoided a hidden pit, and Pip Thistlewick was caught in a snare and left dangling ten feet in the air before being rescued.

00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:01.920
Upon reaching the cavemouth, the party amushed a goblin lookout post hidden in the briars.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:07.120
Despite Zenvon's opening shot going wide, the fight was swift and decisive.

00:01:07.359 --> 00:01:17.439
Varya's magical volleys and firebolts, Sister Maela's mace, Pip's sword, and Zenvon's devastating blowblade strikes brought down two goblins and their boss in short order.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:25.200
The party claimed what weapons they could and pressed into the cave, where Zenvon scouted alone, slipping past a pack of wolves undetected.

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:34.879
Deeper in the darkness, deeper in, the darkness grew absolute, and Zenvon came face to face with a massive coiled snake rearing up from the rubble.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:42.240
